# Architecture

One section per decision. A changed decision gets a new section naming the one it
replaces; the old one stays.

## 1. The repository starts from the agent-harness-config template

**Decision.** {{ project_name }} was created with `copier copy
gh:danielvogler/agent-harness-config --vcs-ref {{ harness_rev }}`. The layout, `Makefile`,
`.pre-commit-config.yaml` and `.github/workflows/` come from the template, and
`.copier-answers.yml` records the answers so `copier update` can bring in newer
conventions.

**Why.** A repository copied by hand from the nearest neighbour inherits that neighbour's
drift. The template produces what the team conventions ask for and nothing more, and the
pinned hooks keep it that way after the first commit.

**Rejected.** Copying files from an existing repository: it carries that repository's
history and quirks. A GitHub template repository: it has no update path once the copy is
made.
